cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Counting time in one's own measurements: the Lorentz c of a time series, verified in Lean"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "AUTHOR-FAMILY-NAME"
    given-names: "AUTHOR-GIVEN-NAMES"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/inc-research/lorentz-c-time-series"
abstract: >-
  A Lean-verified kinematics of the Lorentz c for time series in three state
  variables. For an observer who counts time in its own measurements and takes
  its unit from its own window, every covering window has exactly one Lorentz c,
  with sqrt(3) <= c <= sqrt(N), independent of the units of the axes. Between
  observers, cross-speeds in a frozen unit decide when two observers share one
  cone, and Ignatowsky's theorem in 1+1 shows that a family of frame changes has
  exactly one invariant-speed parameter.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Lorentz transformation
  - time series
  - invariant speed
  - Ignatowsky theorem
